{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When HaShem enlarges, etc.</b> The explanation is that since HaShem was strict with those who craved a craving to eat meat in the wilderness (Numbers 11), and the cravers were buried, from that time onward the craving for meat stood under prohibition. Therefore He said <b>When HaShem enlarges</b>, etc., <b>and you shall say</b>, etc. — meaning: even though you say explicitly that you want to eat meat, and this resembles the statement of the cravers who said ״מִי יַאֲכִלֵנוּ בָּשָׂר״, and He also said <b>when your soul craves</b>, which resembles what is said of the cravers, of whom Scripture says ״הִתְאַוּוּ תַּאֲוָה״ — even so, Scripture permits it to them and said <b>you may eat meat, according to every craving of your soul.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:51.931894219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}